  "body": "A new MCP tool, `detect_holes {name}`, fills a Drill, Bore or Thread operation's hole list from its source model, through the same rule as the app's Detect holes button. Before, an agent's drill on a model with holes always refused \"no holes to drill\".\n\n### What was wrong (`main` 8f30bee and 8cf3c90)\n\n- The drilling kinds machine only the holes stored in their parameters. Only the UI's `State::detect_holes` filled them; the MCP tool table had nothing equivalent.\n- Reproduced through `camcraft-cli mcp` on `testdata/models/Milling-test.step` (see #312).\n\n### What changed\n\n- `operation::detect_holes(world, name, params, setup, src)` (`operation/material.rs`): the rule moved out of the UI unchanged. It reads the source now (`holes_of`), fills whichever list the kind has, adds the drill's radial list on a turret machine (`cross_holes_of`), and refuses by name.\n- `State::detect_holes` calls it: the same refusal texts and the same draft rule, with 55 lines of duplicated logic gone.\n- MCP `detect_holes`: calls it and executes one undoable `EditOperationParams`. It answers `{operation, holes, radial_holes, status}`.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/312-mcp-detect-holes.md`.\n\n### Tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp.rs`: `detect_holes_fills_a_drill_from_its_model_and_undo_empties_it`. A 20 mm disc with a 6 mm blind bore, as STL (the bore suites' `common::bore::revolve`):\n  - the drill refuses \"no holes\" before detection;\n  - `detect_holes` finds 1 axial and 0 radial holes, stored in the drill's params;\n  - the drill generates;\n  - two undos (the generation, then the detection) empty the list;\n  - a Face op is refused \"not a drilling operation\".\n- `handshake_and_tool_list` now expects `detect_holes`.\n- With the tool row taken back out (`git stash` of `tools.rs`), the new test fails: \"unknown tool 'detect_holes'\". The UI's `detect_holes_refuses_recognizes_and_undo_empties_again` passes through the shared rule.\n\n### What ran (Windows 10, local, built from upstream `main` 8cf3c90 plus this commit)\n\n- The quick gate's plan for this diff (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -DryRun`, run by hand with `-j 3`): app lib, `mcp`, `turning`, `turning_profile` (104 pass), and ui lib, `boundary`, `boundary_picks`, `feedback`, `fixtures`, `gpu_render`, `machine`, `models`, `operations`, `shell` (366 pass, 2 ignored).\n- The only failures are the three ui pixel snapshots, with the same pixel counts as clean `main` on this machine (1544, 1815, 2080). The owner's reviewer saw them pass on its own machine (#276's review).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Not run: the windowed app's Detect holes button by hand, Linux, macOS.\n\nChangelog: The MCP server's new detect_holes tool fills a Drill, Bore or Thread operation's holes from its model, the same way the app's Detect holes button does (#312)\n\nFixes #312\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
